{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 24, :comments ["<b>To the one ring.</b> To that ring which was in the thickness of the corner plank — which is equal in placement to the width of the side planks. For in that thickness there was one ring above, aligned with the line of rings of the upper side planks, and one ring in that same thickness below, aligned with the line of rings of the lower side planks. The bars would enter the ring in the thickness of the corner plank together with the rings of the side planks, above and below. Through this the western wall was joined to the northern and to the southern."], :book :exodus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:27:21.775355136Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}